@startuml Import chain

!pragma teoz true

title Import chain (gontroller): every participant is a chain step (own goroutine), every arrow is a channel

control "fswalker\n(entry point)" as Walker

box "providers, one after another (claim: own grouper, or on)" #LightCyan
control "Apple Photos\n(claim + grouper)" as Photos
control "next provider..." as Next
control "generic\n(plain folder)" as Generic
end box

control "files gate" as Gate #LightGreen
control "exif\n(N workers)" as Exif
control "mime" as Mime
control "validator" as Validator #LightGreen

control "cheap preview" as Preview #LightYellow

control "plugins\n(core, then external)" as Plugins
database "DB" as DB
control "closer" as Closer

== files flow in; groups flow out one by one, steps run concurrently ==

loop every file under the root
    Walker -> Photos: file (path, stat)
    note left of Walker
    Unreadable directory:
    skipped, recorded (V1)
    end note
end

alt Apple claims it (inside *.photoslibrary)
    Photos -> Photos: first file: asset links from Photos.sqlite\n(original, render, Live Photo video); buffer of open\ngroups, a group goes out when all its files arrived
    Photos -> Gate: group (asset UUID)
else not claimed: on to the next provider (Immich, ... later)
    Photos -> Next: file
    Next -> Generic: file (nobody claimed it)
    Generic -> Generic: sidecars by name, next to each other\n(buffer: one open group; a complete group goes out)
    Generic -> Gate: group
end
note over Photos: a provider not enabled is not in the chain:\nits files are a plain folder's

Gate -> DB: stat vs files table,\nCheckTime of every file
alt unchanged and the item is Ready
    Gate ->x Gate: drop
else new / changed / not Ready
    Gate -> Exif: group
end

Exif -> Mime: group + exif
Mime -> Mime: kind of every file\n(exif FileType/MIMEType, own extension table,\ncontent sniff), rank: main file
Mime -> Validator: ranked group

Validator -> DB: hash of the main file:\nsame / changed / moved / duplicate
Validator -> Preview: item (GUID) + group

Preview -> Preview: what the browser shows now, no transcode:\nthe main file (JPEG, PNG, ...; H.264 video) /\nthe biggest viewable derivative / an embedded preview\n(exiftool -b into the cache); any size counts
Preview -> Plugins: item + preview ("" = nothing yet)
Plugins -> Closer: item + metadata
Closer -> DB: Visible (a preview) or Waiting (none)
note right of Closer
The client gets Visible (and Ready)
items at once. Ready comes later from
the expensive chain (transcode, fed
from the DB; roadmap: thumbnails)
end note

== end of walk ==

Walker -> Photos: marker (walk result)
Photos -> Next: marker
Next -> Generic: marker
note right of Photos: every step: to its grouper and on
Generic -> Gate: last groups, marker
Photos -> Gate: last groups, marker
Gate -> DB: after the marker from every branch:\ndeletions (V2), only after a complete walk,\nnot under unreadable directories
Closer --> Walker: the last group of the walk is done (items + errors counted)
Walker -> Walker: rescan pause (1 min), then walk again

== One asset again (Apple Photos on demand) ==
note over Photos: Photos made a file of an asset local\n(the viewer asked for it: PhotoKit)
Photos -> Photos: Regroup(uuid): the last load's DB rows\n+ the disk now (no walk, no DB read)
Photos -> Gate: group (asset UUID): like any group,\nonly what changed passes; no marker,\ndeletions untouched
Closer --> Photos: the item is done: the request waiting\nfor it answers (importer Refresh)

@enduml
